; The negative direction of `exclusive-multi-key-exactly-one`, which uses
; this exact schema to show the `:from`+`:to` bundle accepted. Here the
; author supplies that bundle AND `:at`, so two alternatives of the group
; are live at once.
;
; A group is about the alternatives, not the keys: each key is
; `:optional true` on its own, so nothing here is individually wrong. The
; diagnostic exists precisely because per-key checks cannot see the
; constraint.
(plugin :name routes :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name route
    (key :name from :type symbol :optional true)
    (key :name to :type symbol :optional true)
    (key :name at :type symbol :optional true)
    (exclusive-group :cardinality exactly-one
      (alt :keys [from to])
      (alt :keys [at]))))

(route :from a :to b :at c)
